WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.662
Good morning, it's Friday, November 20.

00:00:02.731 --> 00:00:09.898
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:19.660
Today: Sovereign AI turns into a product catalogue, Microsoft sells cheaper task-specific models, and OVHcloud ships Olala with AI Act papers.

00:00:19.729 --> 00:00:21.640
First, the story of the day.

00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:31.538
Microsoft announced at its Ignite event previews that let Foundry open-weight models and agents run on customers' own Azure Kubernetes clusters.

00:00:31.607 --> 00:00:45.601
On November nineteenth in Paris, OVHcloud announced 55 cloud and AI launches, from GPUs to its own Olala model family and an agentic workspace, plus a partnership with Qwant, Shadow and the EUSP web index.

00:00:45.669 --> 00:00:49.970
OVHcloud's page points to its Labs for trying several products.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:56.180
What this really signals: sovereignty is turning into a catalogue with two shapes.

00:00:56.248 --> 00:01:03.911
Hyperscaler software now comes to your own cluster, and a European provider offers every layer, models included.

00:01:03.979 --> 00:01:11.573
Each shape fails differently: dependence on a vendor's control plane, or on a young model with no track record.

00:01:11.642 --> 00:01:20.673
For a platform team, the practical answer is a gateway that treats both as routes, scored on one evaluation set and one price sheet.

00:01:20.741 --> 00:01:26.830
Worth watching: published prices, quotas and regions, which the announcements leave open.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.994
Next, Models and vendors.

00:01:29.056 --> 00:01:40.379
At Ignite on November seventeenth, Microsoft AI chief executive Mustafa Suleyman said enterprises keep telling him token spend is going through the roof, according to Yahoo Finance.

00:01:40.441 --> 00:01:48.323
Microsoft pitched specialised models for specific tasks, and Copilot Fusion, which orchestrates several models for lower cost.

00:01:48.385 --> 00:01:53.890
TechRepublic tracks which Ignite items are generally available and which remain preview.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:02:01.340
The read here: a vendor is now selling routing as a cost lever, the same logic as your gateway.

00:02:01.413 --> 00:02:04.802
Ask for cost per completed task, not per token.

00:02:04.874 --> 00:02:11.580
And check whether a vendor-side router exposes logs and overrides, or hides the model choice.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.199
Next, Platform.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:25.695
OVHcloud's launch list includes AI Routers, described as a single OpenAI-compatible endpoint for all AI traffic, and AI Fabric, where the GPU becomes an argument of a Python function.

00:02:25.763 --> 00:02:29.838
The launch page links both to OVHcloud Labs for trying them.

00:02:29.906 --> 00:02:32.690
No price appears in the sources reviewed.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:41.424
Reading between the lines: a European cloud shipping its own routing layer shows the gateway becoming a standard product.

00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:47.608
Test an OpenAI-compatible endpoint behind your own gateway for latency, quotas and logging.

00:02:47.675 --> 00:02:51.910
Do not make it a default until prices and limits are published.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:53.638
Next, Regulation.

00:02:53.704 --> 00:03:03.191
OVHcloud announced Olala mini, a seven-billion-parameter mixture-of-experts model with one billion active parameters and a 32000-token context.

00:03:03.257 --> 00:03:12.346
It says the model comes with its weights, base model, technical report and AI Act compliance documentation, open source under Apache 2.0.

00:03:12.412 --> 00:03:19.710
It was trained on Jupiter, MeluXina and Jean Zay, with public compute support worth about seven million euros.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:26.291
Why it matters: shipping AI Act documentation with the weights is the practice to copy.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.585
For a retailer choosing an open model, the paperwork is part of the product.

00:03:31.654 --> 00:03:38.460
Small models suit classification and routing, but vendor speed claims are not your quality results.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:39.899
A follow-up.

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:46.611
Expected: Anthropic's first trade on November nineteenth after pricing at eighty-three dollars.

00:03:46.681 --> 00:03:57.238
Result: shares opened at 111 dollars 50, then closed at 97 dollars 17, up 17 percent, in a volatile session on a falling market, according to NBC News.

00:03:57.308 --> 00:03:58.846
The number of the day.

00:03:58.916 --> 00:03:59.685
Fifty-five.

00:03:59.755 --> 00:04:05.209
That is how many cloud and AI launches OVHcloud announced in one day in Paris.

00:04:05.279 --> 00:04:12.410
It shows breadth, not readiness: sort each launch into orderable, beta or roadmap before comparing it.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.459
What to watch.

00:04:13.529 --> 00:04:17.025
Microsoft Ignite closes today, November twentieth.

00:04:17.095 --> 00:04:24.156
Walmart's Agent Profiles are due about November twenty-first, and nothing yet confirms they are live.

00:04:24.226 --> 00:04:37.021
Then Carbon's introductory price ends November thirtieth, Gemini 2.5 requests reroute December first, AI Act marking starts December second, and EuroHPC's Lot 2 closes December third.

00:04:37.091 --> 00:04:41.286
Also watch for prices and quotas on OVHcloud's new products.

00:04:41.356 --> 00:04:43.383
And a question for your team.

00:04:43.453 --> 00:04:54.919
If sovereign options arrive as different shapes, would your gateway score all of them on one evaluation set and one price sheet, or only the vendor you already use?

00:04:54.989 --> 00:04:56.388
That's it for today.

00:04:56.457 --> 00:04:59.184
Sources are in the episode description.

00:04:59.254 --> 00:05:01.352
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:05:01.422 --> 00:05:02.680
See you on Monday.
